I think it's the only thing that matters. An abbreviation is an
abbreviation only when the conversers know that it's an abbreviation for
something else that they both know. Otherwise, it's simply an expansion.
We have to call certain concepts reasonably primitive, and only the
speakers are qualified to announce what they are using as primitives.



